with open('WORKLOG.md', 'a', encoding='utf-8') as f:
    f.write('\n---\n\n## 2026-09-30\n\n### 🐛 Fix: Persist calculated polygon distances immediately upon Apply Geofence\n**Files:** `frontend/src/jsx/components/CommonMaster/AreaCreation.jsx`, `backend/area_app/models.py`\n\n- Fixed an issue where individual polygon distances were missing or incorrectly calculated during AreaGeofenceHistory persistence.\n- Repurposed the existing frontend distance calculation (already used by the UI map) to extract segment data, strip zero-width characters, and format a clean `polygon_distances` array.\n- Updated `saveManualLocation` in `AreaCreation.jsx` to immediately send a POST request to `/api/geofence-history/` upon clicking "Apply Geofence", ensuring the history record and distances are securely persisted in real-time.\n- Simplified `AreaGeofenceHistory.save()` in the backend, removing the synchronous, failure-prone `googlemaps.reverse_geocode` recalculation loop. The backend now strictly respects and stores the frontend-calculated array without overwriting it.\n\n*Last updated: 2026-09-30 16:05 IST*\n')
